Package: omnitiler
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, kwin-wayland (>= 4:6.6) | kwin-x11 (>= 4:6.6), hicolor-icon-theme, libkf6config-bin, libkf6kcmutils-bin
Recommends: omnitiler-native-effect
Description: COSMIC-style automatic tiling for KWin (core with Settings)
 Core of OmniTiler: the KWin script (prebuilt, no Node needed at
 packaging time), the Rust planner/tray binary with on-demand D-Bus plus
 systemd user activation, the application icon, and both native settings
 pages (the effect settings page and the native script settings page, the
 Configure page referenced by the KWin script). The settings pages are
 KWin-independent (Qt/KF6 only, built settings-only with no kwin-dev); the
 effect reconfigure tolerates an absent effect. The active-border effect
 itself lives in the omnitiler-native-effect companion, built against and
 exactly pinned to one KWin distro build.
 .
 Tiling and Settings work with this package alone.
 .
 Revert before removing: open Settings and press Revert (Revert Shortcuts,
 plus Revert to KDE default on any changed host row) to restore host keys
 and shortcut overrides. Removal does not restore them; Settings lives in
 this package, so press Revert before removing it. If you already removed
 without reverting, reinstall this package and press Revert. Disabling the
 script is separate.

Package: omnitiler-native-effect
Architecture: any
Build-Profiles: <!noeffect>
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, omnitiler (= ${source:Version}), libkwin6 (= ${kwin:Version})
Description: OmniTiler native KWin effect (active border)
 Optional ABI-bound companion: the native active-border effect only, built
 against the exact KWin distro build it depends on (libkwin6, including
 the Debian revision, resolved at build time). After a KWin upgrade,
 install the rebuilt companion before relying on the effect: the effect's
 factory IID carries the KWin version it was built against, and a
 mismatched KWin refuses the plugin before instantiation.
 .
 The settings pages (with Revert) live in the core omnitiler package, so
 removing this companion alone leaves Settings and Revert available. Core
 tiling works without it.
 .
 Revert before removing core: no Revert step is lost by removing this
 package alone (Settings stays in core). Removal does not restore host keys
 or shortcut overrides; press Revert in the core Settings before removing
 core. If you already removed core without reverting, reinstall core and
 press Revert.
